  "adaptations": "1) cheap CPU smoke uses a SYNTHETIC graded codebook (build_graded_codebook) not the spiking HomeostaticAssocGraph learn (the real GPU run uses --cortex learned); both expose the same {word: graded_code}. 2) grounded_codes wants phases in [0,1)^D, so the DG decorrelating encode's binary expansion is mapped to D decorrelated phases via a fixed random projection->angle. 3) the GPU-validated BridgeParser is bypassed for the gates (explicit-roles store_fact); the matrix queries are composer-delegated and parser-independent (the parser is covered by the existing matrix test suite)."
